>>
Rule 1 (input tensor to from_dlpack should have non-zero dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (from_dlpack requires the input tensor to have at least one element if the number of dimensions is greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 3 (dtype of input tensor should be a valid dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 12
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor should have positive shape values along its dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 5 (If input tensor v_1 is a bool tensor, all values must be true or false)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then (min(v_1) = 0 ∧ max(v_1) = 1)
>>
Rule 6 (If the input tensor v_1 is complex, the real and imaginary parts should be finite)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 then min(v_1) > -10000000000 ∧ max(v_1) < 10000000000
>>
Rule 7 (If input is a str type, then its values should be selected from the defined string list.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (min(v_1) = "ii" ∨ min(v_1) = "ii->i" ∨ min(v_1) = "i,j->ij" ∨ min(v_1) = "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ min(v_1) = "...ij->...ji" ∨ min(v_1) = "bn,anm,bm->ba" ∨ min(v_1) = "none" ∨ min(v_1) = "mean" ∨ min(v_1) = "sum" ∨ min(v_1) = "max" ∨ min(v_1) = "constant" ∨ min(v_1) = "tanh")
>>
Rule 8 (If input tensor has more than 2 dimensions, then its last two dimensions should be greater than 0)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) > 0
>>
Rule 9 (The minimum value of the input tensor should be less than or equal to the maximum value of the tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 10 (If input tensor is an integer type, then its value should be within the range of int64)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 then min(v_1) ≥ -9223372036854775808 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 9223372036854775807
>>
Rule 11 (If the input tensor is uint8 then max value should be less than or equal to 255 and min value should be greater or equal to 0)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 255
>>
Rule 12 (If the input tensor has a shape of (1,), the minimum value must be less than or equal to the maximum value)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 then min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 13 (If the input tensor is float16, then the minimum value must be greater than or equal to -65504 and the maximum value must be less than or equal to 65504)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 6 then min(v_1) ≥ -65504 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 65504
>>
Rule 14 (If input tensor dtype is not supported, throw an error)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 13
>>
Rule 15 (If the input tensor v_1 is of type np.int8, then all values must be within the range [-128, 127])
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 1 then min(v_1) ≥ -128 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 127
>>
Rule 16 (If input tensor has one or more dimensions the product of all its dimensions must not be zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) = false
>>
Rule 17 (If the input tensor has only one dimension, its shape must be greater than zero.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 18 (The shape of input tensor should not exceed 2^31 - 1, which is the maximum value of int32)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) < 2147483647
>>
Rule 19 (If the input tensor v_1 is of type np.int16, then all values must be within the range [-32768, 32767])
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 2 then min(v_1) ≥ -32768 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 32767
>>
Rule 20 (The shape of the input tensor should be non-empty (not an empty tuple))
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 21 (If the tensor v_1 has a specified dtype, then that dtype needs to be valid as well)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 12 then true
